                                        <width>42</width>
                                        <depth>38</depth>
                                    </dimensions>
                                </support>
                            </supportDesc>
                            <layoutDesc>
                                <layout>
                                    <p>Altar with relief on three faces: seated goddess with scepter (right), Hermes with caduceus (left), Men on horseback going right at gallop (back). Main inscribed face records Artemon son of Ailios and then Rhopson son of Neoges Sophos, assistant of Men Kleinas, who dedicated cult furnishings from his own funds.</p>
                                    <rs ref="http://www.eagle-network.eu/voc/writing/lod/1">incisa a scalpello</rs>
                                </layout>
